{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":18365,"duration_api_ms":19576,"num_turns":7,"result":"I wrote `src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`. I haven't run it.\n\nIt hooks `tracepoint:power:cpu_frequency`. For each frequency change it prints the time, CPU, old frequency and new frequency in MHz. On Ctrl-C it prints the number of changes per CPU and a per-CPU histogram of frequencies.\n\nThe first change on each CPU shows an old frequency of 0, because there's no earlier value to compare against.\n\nRun it with:\n```bash\nsudo bpftrace src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt\n```\n\nSome drivers, such as `intel_pstate` in active mode and `amd-pstate-epp`, change frequency in hardware. They don't fire this tracepoint, so the script would print nothing there.\n\nI haven't added a README or a SUMMARY.md entry. I can add them if you want.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d04b1c0e-8d51-448d-b200-b307d084263f","total_cost_usd":0.07050384999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2129,"cache_read_input_tokens":128477,"output_tokens":1566,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2129},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":289,"cache_read_input_tokens":26542,"cache_creation_input_tokens":865,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":865,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":351,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000451,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":12,"outputTokens":1566,"cacheReadInputTokens":128477,"cacheCreationInputTokens":2129,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.07005284999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":